<title>UK: UK manufacturing rises 0.2% in Dec.</title>
<headline>UK manufacturing rises 0.2% in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following seasonally adjusted data on UK industrial production in December:</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING OUTPUT	    DEC     NOV	(PREL NOV)</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	   +0.2    -0.3     (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	     +1.4    +0.5     (+0.2)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		+0.6    +0.6     (+0.4)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   +0.9    +0.5     (+0.3)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 102.7   102.5    (102.2)</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change in pct  +0.6    +0.6     (+0.4)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	     +1.9    +1.7     (+1.3)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		+0.9    +0.7     (+0.6)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   +1.7    +1.2     (+1.0)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 108.8   108.1    (107.7)</p>
<p>MINING/QUARRYING INCLUDING OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	   +2.1    +3.2     (+2.7)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	     +4.6    +5.6     (+5.2)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		+2.0    +1.0     (+0.8)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   +4.3    +2.6     (+2.5)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 149.8   146.7    (146.1)</p>
<p>ELECTRICITY, GAS AND WATER</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	   +2.2    +5.4     (+5.0)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	     +2.4    +7.1     (+6.8)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		+2.7    +1.6     (+1.5)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   +5.5    +5.9     (+5.8)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 128.5   125.8    (125.4)</p>
<p>OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		+2.4    N/A	(+0.8)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   +6.3    N/A	(+4.0)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 188.3   183.1    (181.9)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast was for industrial production to rise by 0.5 percent in December, for a year-on-year rise of 1.3 percent. Manufacturing output was expected to rise 0.3 percent on the month and 1.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>The ONS said that for 1996 as a whole, production industries' output was 1.2 percent higher than in 1995. Within that, the mining and quarrying industries, including oil and gas extraction, increased by 3.1 percent, manufacturing output increased by 0.5 percent and electricity, gas and water supply industries increased by 5.2 percent.</p>
